{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And he took up his discourse.</b> It is like תּוֹעֲפַת רְאֵם קַרְנָיִם (Numbers 23:22), לְבִיא (Numbers 23:24), יָקוּם (Numbers 23:24)." "<b>Hear, my witness.</b> From the root עד, and so לֹא שְׁבַתֶּם עֵדִי, and the meaning is doubled. The vav in עֵדִי is added, like לְמַעְיְנוּ מָיִם." "And the meaning of <b>not a man is El.</b> Because he said וְקַבְּנוּ לִי מִשָּׁם, and he had already said לֹא קָבַּה אֵל."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The Hebrew lists four scriptural words/phrases with no connective tissue; each parallels usage in Balaam's oracles. Translated hyper-literally.", 1 "The reference לא שבתם עדי is likely to Genesis 21:30 or a similar verse where עד appears with a possessive suffix."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:14.797634971Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}